<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="ready-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="ready-title">Signs you may be ready</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>Books are current, and closed each month</li>
        <li>You make decisions on hiring, pricing or expansion that depend on figures</li>
        <li>Cash feels tight even in months with good sales</li>
        <li>A bank or investor expects forecasts</li>
        <li>You have several products or locations, and cannot see which make money</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Signs you are not ready</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list tick-list--no plain-list">
        <li>Your books are months behind. Start with {% routeLink "/services/accounting-bookkeeping/", "bookkeeping" %}</li>
        <li>You want someone to "sort out GST". That is compliance work</li>
        <li>You want a loan arranged. Ask what they will actually do</li>
        <li>You will not act on what you are told</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="month-title">
  <div class="wrap layout-side">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="month-title" class="first-h2">What you should receive</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>A monthly one-page review:</strong> sales, margin, cash, and what changed and why.</li>
        <li><strong>A rolling cash forecast:</strong> 13 weeks is a common format, showing when money may run short.</li>
        <li><strong>A budget against actuals,</strong> with explanations of large differences.</li>
        <li><strong>Unit economics:</strong> what you make per product, customer or location.</li>
        <li><strong>A short meeting,</strong> with decisions and owners written down.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>If you only get a long pack with no recommendation, you are paying for a report.</p>

      <h2 id="limits">Limits to keep in mind</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A virtual CFO cannot promise profits, funding or valuations.</li>
        <li>Decisions and legal responsibility stay with the owners and directors.</li>
        <li>Part-time means part-time. Ask how much attention you get, and how quickly they respond.</li>
        <li>Investment or securities advice may need separate registration, so ask before relying on it.</li>
        <li>The role does not replace filings, audit or legal advice.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="ask">Questions to ask</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Show me a redacted example of what you send a client like me.</li>
        <li>What decision did your work change for a client, and how?</li>
        <li>Who actually does the work: you, or a junior?</li>
        <li>What do you need from my team each month?</li>
        <li>How will we know within six months if this is worth it?</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="fees">What affects the fee</h2>
      <p>Hours or scope, business complexity, number of entities, the quality of your current books, and how often you meet. Ask for a defined scope, the fee and exit terms in writing.</p>
